Package: SGDrivE
Title: Screwworm Genetic-Control Dynamics Explorer
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Prateek", "Verma", , "prateekverma@berkeley.edu", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Simulates genotype-resolved population dynamics of the New
    World screwworm (Cochliomyia hominivorax) under genetic control, such
    as the sterile insect technique, precision-guided sterile insect
    technique, female-specific release of insects carrying a dominant
    lethal, and gene drives. Life-history biology follows the
    temperature-driven physiologically based demographic model of
    Gutierrez and Ponti (2014) <doi:10.1111/afe.12046>. Inheritance is
    read from 'MGDrivE' inheritance cubes (Sanchez et al. 2020
    <doi:10.1111/2041-210X.13318>) and mating follows the unmated/mated
    structure of 'MGDrivE2' (Wu et al. 2021
    <doi:10.1371/journal.pcbi.1009030>). Deterministic (ordinary
    differential equation) and stochastic (chain-binomial) solvers share
    a single 'C++' rate kernel.
